      "answer": "It usually kicks off when someone decides a meeting needs to happen, though the exact trigger can vary depending on the situation."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q2",
      "question": "What system or method does the organizer currently use to check room availability — for instance, a shared calendar, a dedicated booking platform, or a physical sign-up sheet?",
      "answer": "There's generally some kind of tool or method used to look into whether a space is free, but specifics aren't really pinned down."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q3",
      "question": "If the preferred room is not available at the requested time, what steps does the organizer take — do they select an alternative room, propose a different time, or follow an escalation path?",
      "answer": "When something isn't available, the person in charge typically figures out an alternative somehow, though the exact approach tends to differ."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q4",
      "question": "How are participants informed of the confirmed room details — is this done through an automatic calendar invitation, a manual email, a messaging tool, or another channel?",
      "answer": "People involved usually get word of the details through some communication channel or another, but the specific method isn't really defined."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q5",
      "question": "What is the process when a reserved meeting is cancelled or rescheduled — who is responsible for releasing the room, and how is that action carried out?",
      "answer": "Generally someone handles releasing the space when things change, though who does it and how isn't particularly specified."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q6",
      "question": "Is any employee permitted to reserve a meeting room, or are there role-based restrictions or an approval step required before a reservation is confirmed?",
      "answer": "There may or may not be restrictions depending on circumstances, but nothing specific about roles or approvals is really spelled out."
    }
  ]
}
